    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a Luhn check digit over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, following the project's derived-field pattern (computed at response time in the mapper, not persisted).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Luhn.java`** (new, in `rest/function/common/`) \u2014 a small utility with `checkDigit(String)` that computes the Luhn check digit over only the digit characters of the input, ignoring the `CITY3-LAST3-` letters. It mirrors the reference algorithm the acceptance test uses exactly (doubling from the rightmost digit, `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`), and null-guards to `0`.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `checkDigit` field (integer 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, right after `customerCode`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `checkDigit` that calls `Luhn.checkDigit(owner.getCustomerCode())`, alongside the other derived mappings.\n\nThe new `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` test \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact `checkDigit` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green.",
